{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/69655-rules","id":69655,"title":"Rules...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-10T23:43:46-08:00","id":69655,"title":"Rules...","content":"So after running a demo of forsaken (manitou springs) my group decided they liked the dice rules for forsaken far better than apocalypse (makes sense what with how much simpler it is). Conversion isn't an issue for most of it, my only problem is one of my players is a Nuwisha, and I'm having a hard time how to convert his nonsense over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T00:07:43-08:00","id":69662,"title":"","content":"War Against the Pure, if you have it, offers some great options for making custom shifters of different stripes. There's a were-coyote in the Changing Breeds book but I'd steer clear of them, the rules/mechanics of it are pretty up in the air. Failing that, the Werewolf Translation Guide may have a means for a more direct port over?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T00:59:24-08:00","id":69682,"title":"","content":"The Translation Guide isn't going to help with the Fera. Honestly though, the Nuwisha are the easiest Fera to just make into werewolves. Forsaken, since it doesn't have breeding with wolves as part of the dynamic, already has the option for Uratha to adapt to the appearance of the local canid populations.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to translate a Nuwisha you can either use one of the non-wolf shifter books Nickpire84 mentioned, or you can make them a werewolf and let the Nuwisha player be part of a Lodge with a coyote Totem to accent the special trickster stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T04:19:00-08:00","id":69748,"title":"","content":"My recomendation:<br /> <br /> Use War against the Pure rules to create the basic Nuwisha template (the forms and their modifiers). Mine both Skinchangers (the chapter about the Siten Uzu) and maybe Changing Breeds for example powers (you can easily turn Aspects into Gifts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T07:10:36-08:00","id":69822,"title":"","content":"Awhile back, Stew Wilson wrote something about this in his blog. I've saved it to a Word Document and it might be what you're looking for. I'll copy and paste it below.<br /> <br /> &quot;The <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/100710/Werewolf-Translation-Guide&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Werewolf Translation Guide</b></a> had to focus on the werewolves at the heart of both <b>Apocalypse</b> and <b>Forsaken</b>, and didn\u2019t have the space to talk about alternative shapeshifters. I know that the Fera of <b>Apocalypse</b> have a lot of fans (myself included), so I got permission to take the bare-bones conversion rules from the first draft and release them online.<br /> The following system is a rough guide for converting the Fera as given in the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3364/Players-Guide-to-the-Changing-Breeds?it=1&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Player\u2019s Guide to the Changing Breeds</b></a>. Naturally, these rules are guidelines. The results need to meet with the approval of the group before seeing play. If you want further inspiration for introducing Fera-like shapeshifters into <b>Forsaken</b>, shapeshifters get a whole section in <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/25702/The-War-Against-the-Pure?it=1&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>War Against the Pure</b></a> that provides a good starting point.<br /> These rules should leave the shapeshifters with an approximate power level the same as the Uratha. If you want to enhance that, see the options presented in the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/100710/Werewolf-Translation-Guide&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Werewolf Translation Guide</b></a>.<br /> <br /> <b>Step One: Convert Traits</b><br /> Converting the Trait modifiers of a given Fera\u2019s forms involves a few changes:<ul><li>Subtract 1 from form bonuses to Strength and Stamina.</li> <li>Don\u2019t modify the Dexterity bonus.</li> <li>Apply the more severe of any Appearance and Manipulation penalty to Manipulation.</li> <li>Any Perception bonus remains the same, and applies to Wits</li> <li>\u201cNear\u201d forms that are significantly larger than humans get Size +1.</li> <li>Animal forms have Size appropriate for the animal in question, p. XX of the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/1124/World-of-Darkness-Rulebook?it=1&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>World of Darkness Rulebook</b></a> can provide guidelines.</li> <li>Crinos-equivalent forms have Size +2 (+1 if the Breed is noted for their small Crinos-equivalents) and 1/1 natural armor.</li> </ul><br /> Changes to Attributes and Size affect Initiative, Speed, Health, Defense, and other derived traits as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Step Two: Natural Weapons</b><br /> The options available to the Fera will vary a lot by form. The most common set includes: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">War-Form</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Bite +2L, Claw +1L</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Near-Beast</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Bite +2L, Claw +0L</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Beast</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Bite +2L</td> </tr> </table></div> Some Fera have claw attacks in Near-Human, which deal +0L, or claws in Beast form that deal +0L (often alongside a bite that only does +1L). As a rough guide: if an attack is likely to fuck up a human being, it deals +2 lethal damage. If it\u2019s going to ruin his day but may need a couple of hits to really bring the pain, it deals +1 lethal damage. If it\u2019s sharp and pointy but fundamentally no worse than a kitchen knife, it deals +0 lethal damage. All forms from War-Form to Beast can bite without grappling first.<br /> <br /> <b>Step Three: Lunacy</b><br /> War-Form and both Near-forms (where present) incite Lunacy much the same as werewolves. If a form specifically gives a bonus to witnesses resisting Delirium, apply each \u201cstep\u201d of reduced Delirium as an effective +1 to the victim\u2019s Willpower when it comes to resisting Lunacy. This bonus is cumulative with form-specific modifiers\u2014a Breed that reduces normal Delirium by 1 step in their War-Form would give a +1 Willpower bonus in War-Form and a +5 bonus when in Near-Human.<br /> <br /> <b>Step Four: Gifts and Rites</b><br /> Gifts and Rites convert using the systems starting on pp. 22 of the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/100710/Werewolf-Translation-Guide&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Werewolf Translation Guide</b></a>.<br /> <br /> <b>Step Five: Renown</b><br /> Fera use a range of categories of Renown, detailed in the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3364/Players-Guide-to-the-Changing-Breeds?it=1&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Player\u2019s Guide to the Changing Breeds</b></a>. Use those writeups, along with the example of Apocalypse-centric Purity Renown on p. 33 of the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/100710/Werewolf-Translation-Guide&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Werewolf Translation Guide</b></a> to convert Renown as needed.<br /> <br /> <b>Step Six: Details</b><br /> This section covers specifics for each breed. Bits that aren\u2019t covered either have no system (Corax eye-drinking) or the system in <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3364/Players-Guide-to-the-Changing-Breeds?it=1&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Player\u2019s Guide to the Changing Breeds</b></a> doesn\u2019t need changing (Kitsune not regenerating).<br /> <br /> <b>Ananasi:</b> Pithus form counts as Near-Beast for everything already stated. Crawlerling form creates a swarm of radius equal to the Ananasi\u2019s Size in yards (Swarms are covered on p. 198 of <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/55727/World-of-Darkness:-Innocents?it=1&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>World of Darkness Innocents</b></a>). When a swarm takes enough damage to reduce it to half its original radius, the character will look and act rather differently. Ananasi webs have Durability 3, Size 1, Structure 8, Damage 2 (only for grappling). Were-spiders only regain Essence when doing damage with a bite attack, each point of damage inflicted causes them to regain a point of Essence. Swap the modifiers for Stepping Sideways in built-up and rural areas. Ananasi don\u2019t regenerate but can spend Essence to heal bashing or lethal damage at a rate of one point per point of damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Corax:</b> In Crinos form, Corax have a Flight speed equal to their land speed + 5; in Corvid form, increase Speed by 5, but they don\u2019t really have a walking Speed\u2014most birds have a species factor of 10 when calculating flight speed, rather than the 5 common among land creatures. Hollow bones gives +2 dice to Athletics rolls in Crinos, but attackers wielding weapons that do bashing damage gain +1 die. When distracted by shiny objects, Corax must make a reflexive Resolve + Composure roll to act normally.<br /> <br /> <b>Gurahl:</b> Were-bears raise Strength or Stamina by spending Essence, at a rate of one point per dot per turn. Alternatively, they can increase Health by 1 for the scene by spending 2 points of Essence (but see Temporary Health Dots, p. 173 of the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/1124/World-of-Darkness-Rulebook?it=1&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>World of Darkness Rulebook</b></a>). Add 3 dice to Composure rolls that involve the were-bear\u2019s need to protect, but a Gurahl\u2019s player must spend a point of Willpower if her character ever changes his mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Kitsune:</b> Were-foxes receive an extra dot of Dexterity for free at character creation. This comes before spending Attribute dots, and their human-form maximum is still 5. Kitsune always use the higher of Dexterity or Wits to determine Defense, and don\u2019t take aggravated damage from silver. Were-foxes do inflict Lunacy, but observers have an additional +3 die bonus to their Willpower roll to resist (+5 in total for Juko, and +7 for Sambuhenge)<br /> <br /> <b>Mokole</b>: Aspect benefits translate directly into <b>Forsaken</b> terms. Sum the character\u2019s Harmony and Primal Urge, then divide by two (rounding up). Select that many Archid characteristics. Armor provides 2/2 armor every time it\u2019s taken. Color Change adds three dice to contested Stealth rolls when the Mokole is hiding. Bladed Tail/Horn give an additional means of attack that does +2L damage. Huge Size increases Stamina and Size by +1 (and thus Health by +2) for each pick. Long Teeth/Terrible Claws add 2 dice to bite and claw attacks. Poison Sacs deliver a Toxicity 4 poison. Other Archid characteristics don\u2019t need changing.<br /> <br /> <b>Nagah:</b> Regain Essence when underwater. Primal Urge is not harder to raise; it\u2019s plenty expensive enough. Nagah venom is a Toxicity 6 poison.<br /> <br /> <b>Nuwisha:</b> Do not take aggravated damage from silver and cannot frenzy. Their Primal Urge trait measures their closeness to Coyote, as such they don\u2019t suffer social modifiers for having a high Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> <b>Ratkin:</b> Blood Memory requires a Harmony roll, with a penalty depending on the specific nature of what the rat-shifter is after (difficulty conversions are provided on p. 29 of the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/100710/Werewolf-Translation-Guide&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Werewolf Translation Guide</b></a>). Ratkin blood is a Toxicity 3 poison, anyone consuming it also suffers the effects of a dose of hallucinogenic drugs. Pretty much all Aspect traits convert directly.<br /> <br /> <b>Rokea:</b> Shark-born Rokea suffer a -3 penalty to Presence and Manipulation rolls when dealing with humans. Worse, any dice that show a \u20181\u2019 also subtract a success from the character\u2019s total. Double the Rokea\u2019s Primal Urge when checking to see if the character falls into Death Rage. Chasmus and Gladius both have 1/1 armor, and an attacker who makes a successful unarmed attack against a Rokea in those forms suffers a point of bashing damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hope this helps.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T07:26:37-08:00","id":69833,"title":"","content":"I started running my werewolf game using Changing Breeds. It is a mechanical and thematic mess in a lot of ways, but the Aspects work pretty well as abilities, and if you aren't afraid to fudge the form adjustments, it can work out.<br /> <br /> For this game, I allowed my Changing Breeds to purchase Gifts, but all were out of tribe (they did get free ones for Renown), except when a lodge I wrote gave them affinity; I did also allow them to &quot;choose a moon phase&quot; and be able to pick up those gifts as affinity, because they were too damn useful to lose. I allowed my Uratha characters to also by CB Aspects if appropriate for wolves. I also offered them a bigger version of AnyBeast, where they could buy it at 4 dots and take on all five forms of another race from Changing Breeds (at ST discretion) (one race per 1/2 Primal Urge) [Not many took this option, though. Only one player, who took the Black Bear forms]. <br /> The *silly* breeds were out, but I've had a were -lion, -fox, -rat, and -bear (black bear) and nothing has been thrown spectacularly out of balance. In my experience, players won't mind if they have a few less dice for form bonuses, if it feels likes they're appropriately playing their breed - with the appropriate strengths and weakness. And as long as no one plays a were-elephant. I imagine Apocalypse veterans will be more cool with this than, from what I've heard, many nwod players.<br /> <br /> Then again, they might also try setting the first copy of the book on fire, because of what it did to Fera thematically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T11:48:47-08:00","id":72748,"title":"","content":"I think i'll just use the combat rules from forsaken or even the gmc combat rules instead of an entire setting switch. I know my players found apocalypse's combat a touch slow with the accuracy roll, plus the damage roll, then the soak roll and after an hour of combat finding out only something like 20 seconds passed between 3 players... yeaaaah. Not to mention all the use of rage and everything else. The basic forsaken rules and their simplification made them as a whole a lot happier. That and Apocalypse has a heavy emphasis on combat, and Forsaken seems to be far more optional in what you do with things. Course it could just be how I'm running it. War wolves don't really give one much of an option though.<br /> <br /> edit: on an unrelated note, what the hell deals aggravated damage in new world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 02-15-2014, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T04:38:27-08:00","id":73131,"title":"","content":"New World, or New New world? Because the revisions tendo to downgrade even more the sources of Aggravated damage (besides the specific banes of the splats, like silver in the case of the Uratha).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T19:19:57-08:00","id":73502,"title":"","content":"uh... core forsaken first. then what the gmc appears to be doing. I kinda understand the werewolves garou form being downgraded from apocalypse to lethal damage, what with them doing animalistic attacks. They also aren't as big though I don't think. My understanding of the apocalypse monster is 9 feet 4-600 pounds of flesh. Forsaken seems to be like... 7... 2-300.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T06:06:01-08:00","id":73679,"title":"","content":"Well, as far as Core Forsaken is concerned there's silver (obviously <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), a four dot Gift called &quot;Savage Rending&quot; (makes your Claw attacks Aggravated against anything) a 3 dot Gift &quot;Silver jaws&quot; that is self-explanatory, and 5 dot Fetish weapons (not all do Aggravated damage, but is one of the posible powers of such weapons).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T06:18:18-08:00","id":73683,"title":"","content":"Size discussion with pictures reference: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/3942-the-size-scale\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...the-size-scale</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}